smb: client: use GFP_KERNEL in get_targets()

jira KERNEL-1962
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9
commit-author Fredric Cover <fredric.cover.lkernel@gmail.com>
commit 031fe051abb3c1f36c2ba6346931fcdb3cddaeae
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.27.1.el9_9/031fe051.failed

Currently, get_targets() uses GFP_ATOMIC to allocate the cache target
iterator and to duplicate t->name. The callers of get_targets() are
in a sleepable context; therefore, switch to GFP_KERNEL to reduce
risk of failure and reduce pressure on emergency pools in low-memory
scenarios.

	Signed-off-by: Fredric Cover <fredric.cover.lkernel@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.org>
(cherry picked from commit 031fe051abb3c1f36c2ba6346931fcdb3cddaeae)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/smb/client/dfs_cache.c
diff --cc fs/smb/client/dfs_cache.c
index dab434d90498,26956e33037e..000000000000
--- a/fs/smb/client/dfs_cache.c
+++ b/fs/smb/client/dfs_cache.c
@@@ -798,7 -798,7 +798,11 @@@ static int get_targets(struct cache_ent
  	INIT_LIST_HEAD(head);
  
  	list_for_each_entry(t, &ce->tlist, list) {
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		it = kzalloc(sizeof(*it), GFP_ATOMIC);
++=======
+ 		it = kzalloc_obj(*it, GFP_KERNEL);
++>>>>>>> 031fe051abb3 (smb: client: use GFP_KERNEL in get_targets())
  		if (!it) {
  			rc = -ENOMEM;
  			goto err_free_it;
* Unmerged path fs/smb/client/dfs_cache.c
